e of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,1),(2,2),(-4,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534354 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-10cf90fb-e29e-510d-8cf4-93075f7dd6be" 17592186420099 "answer-7699eaf3-de8c-5053-898a-a4c8beee968f" 17592186420100 "answer-99a9553b-c748-5118-a8d9-ca0c58ba4325" 17592186420101 "answer-e9ef7977-1930-5dd3-9b84-4d0b1b641d43" 17592186420102 "answer-eadf43e5-1274-5818-a95a-76c46e2e08da" 17592186420103 "answer-field-7fc3ccce-1ebd-5f22-9b8f-6e3842468c4d" 17592186420104 "question-08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054" 17592186420105}}
